      "message": "I was initially going to just rely on the compiler to optimize out the check in `checked_cast` if it wouldn\u0027t be necessary. I would probably do that instead of having our own logic for whether the check is needed even though I\u0027m sure we can get that logic correct.\n\nBut then I figured, why have two checks (checked_cast + hardening check), when we only need one? Which is how I ended up just implementing the checks in Dawn. I didn\u0027t try to check whether the compiler would be able to optimize to combine the two checks.\n\nI don\u0027t have a very strong opinion between the two, so if you think that way is better I\u0027m fine with it.",
